# Runtime artefacts the smoke suites write beside themselves (resource ids recorded between runs,
# and the harness's own tmpfile()). Untracked, but prettier does not read .gitignore, so without
# these a single smoke run leaves prettier-check failing.
#
# Both depths, deliberately. A pattern carrying a path separator is ANCHORED, so
# `tools/smoketest/_*.json` matches only the top directory and not `tools/smoketest/v260/`, where the
# per-wave suites keep their state (`_export_vehicle.json`, `_g5_pre_deploy.json`). Running one v260
# suite otherwise left prettier-check failing on files the next run rewrites anyway. Kept as two lines
# rather than replaced by the `**` form alone so the top-level intent stays readable.
tools/smoketest/_*.json
tools/smoketest/**/_*.json
# MSBuild output for the ArcGIS Pro connector. Its own .gitignore covers bin/ and obj/, which again
# prettier does not consult — building the connector once otherwise reports two generated
# VamsConnector.deps.json files as unformatted forever.
tools/ExternalIntegrations/arcgispro-connector-for-vams/bin
tools/ExternalIntegrations/arcgispro-connector-for-vams/obj

# Seeded live-test fixtures. These are copied third-party sample data and hand-authored probe files
# whose exact bytes are the point of the fixture — a tileset.json's sibling reference, an HTML probe's
# inline script. Reformatting them changes what the fixture tests. Path-anchored with a trailing slash
# so it matches these directories only, not any directory that happens to share the name.
tools/smoketest/_seed_viewers/
tools/smoketest/_seed_3d/
tools/smoketest/_seed_tileset_root/

# Captured add-on API fixtures. An add-on's backend tests keep sanitized request/response captures in
# their fixtures/ directory, and each file must stay byte-for-byte what the add-on's sanitizer emits (its
# tests re-run the sanitizer over every file); reformatting them would fail that guard, so they are
# excluded like the seeded live-test fixtures above.
backend/tests/handlers/addon/*/fixtures/

# Subagent-driven-development workspace (gitignored scratch: ledgers, briefs, reports, review diffs).
# Anchored like /docs above so only the repo-root directory is excluded.
/.superpowers
